# Supabase connection — the only configuration CryoMap needs.
#
# These two values are PUBLIC by design: the URL and the publishable/anon key
# are shipped to the browser, and row-level security (not key secrecy) is the
# real access boundary. There is no service-role key — the app never uses one.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in YOUR OWN Supabase project:
#
#   1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com (or run Supabase locally),
#      then apply the migrations in supabase/migrations/ to it.
#   2. Paste the project's "Project URL" and its publishable (anon) key below.
#
# See docs/SELF_HOSTING.md for the full walkthrough (migrations, Google OAuth).
#
# Never point .env.local at a database with real data — `pnpm dev` reads AND
# writes whatever project it is given. Use your own dev/local project.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_OR_ANON_KEY
